# The container build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT (.github/workflows/containers.yml
# passes `context: .`), because every Dockerfile under containers/ COPYs its pins from
# requirements/ — the same files the workflows install. A per-directory context cannot
# reach outside itself, so the context had to widen; this file keeps what is actually
# uploaded to the builder small.
#
# EXCLUSIONS ONLY, no `*` + re-include pair. The inverted form is one typo away from
# excluding a file some Dockerfile COPYs, and the whole tree is ~10 MB, so there is nothing
# to win by being clever. Add a directory here when it grows, not pre-emptively.
.git
.github
.nextflow
.nf-test
docs
site
work
results
benchmarks
tests/testdata
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
